{"tool_name":"morphographx","contents":["neubias","oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"morphographx","home":"http://www.morphographx.org/","summary":"Cross-platform, open-source application for the visualization and processing of 3D biological datasets.","addition_date":"2017-08-03T18:51:48Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-25T14:50:22.379566Z","tool_type":["Desktop application"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:morphographx","credit":[{"email":"smith@mpipz.mpg.de","name":"Richard Smith","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"],"url":"http://www.mpipz.mpg.de/smith"}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"http://www.mpipz.mpg.de/MorphoGraphX/help"},{"type":["User manual"],"url":"http://www.mpipz.mpg.de/4085950/MGXUserManual.pdf"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Image analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3443"}]}],"name":"MorphoGraphX","operating_system":["Linux"],"owner":"mbs_import","publication":[{"doi":"10.1007/978-1-62703-643-6_10","metadata":{"abstract":"Confocal microscopy is a technique widely used to live-image plant tissue. Cells can be visualized by using fluorescent probes that mark the cell wall or plasma membrane. This enables the confocal microscope to be used as a 3D scanner with submicron precision. Here we present a protocol using the 3D image processing software MorphoGraphX (http://www.MorphoGraphX.org) to extract the surface geometry and cell shapes in the shoot apex. By segmenting cells over consecutive time points, precise growth maps of the shoot apex can be produced. It is also possible to tag a protein of interest with a fluorescent marker and quantify protein expression at the cellular level. \u00a9 2014 Springer Science+Business Media, New York.","authors":[{"name":"De Reuille P.B."},{"name":"Robinson S."},{"name":"Smith R.S."}],"citationCount":25,"date":"2014-01-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Methods in Molecular Biology","title":"Quantifying cell shape and gene expression in the shoot apical meristem using morphographX"},"pmid":"24132424"}],"topic":[{"term":"Cell biology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_2229"},{"term":"Data visualisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0092"},{"term":"Proteins","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0078"},{"term":"Structure analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0081"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"MorphoGraphX","home":"https://bio.tools/morphographx","summary":"Cross-platform, open-source application for the visualization and processing of 3D biological datasets.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:morphographx/app/www.morphographx.org","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"documentation":{"general":true,"manual":true},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":18,"citations":[{"count":1,"year":"2014"},{"count":1,"year":"2015"},{"count":1,"year":"2018"},{"count":1,"year":"2019"},{"count":1,"year":"2020"},{"count":1,"year":"2021"},{"count":1,"year":"2025"},{"count":2,"year":"2022"},{"count":2,"year":"2024"},{"count":3,"year":"2016"},{"count":4,"year":"2017"}],"doi":"10.1007/978-1-62703-643-6_10","pmid":"24132424","ref_count":0,"refs":[],"title":"Quantifying cell shape and gene expression in the shoot apical meristem using MorphoGraphX.","year":2014}]}],"summary":{"description":true},"website":{"bioschemas":false,"copyright":false,"https":true,"license":false,"operational":200,"redirects":[{"status":301,"url":"https://morphographx.org/"},{"status":301,"url":"https://www.morphographx.org/"}],"ssl":true,"ssl_err":null}},"support":{"email":true}},{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/morphographx","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":null,"@type":"metrics","project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"publications":[],"summary":{"description":true},"website":{"bioschemas":false,"copyright":false,"https":true,"license":false,"operational":200,"redirects":[{"status":301,"url":"https://morphographx.org/"},{"status":301,"url":"https://www.morphographx.org/"}],"ssl":true,"ssl_err":null}}}]},"neubias":{"body":[{"format":"basic_html","processed":"<p>MorphoGraphX is a free Linux application for the visualization and analysis of 3D biological datasets. Developed by researchers, it is primarily used for the analysis and quantification of 3D live-imaged confocal data sets.</p>\n\n<p>The main research interests adressed by MorphoGraphX are:</p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>Shape extraction</li>\n\t<li>Growth analysis</li>\n\t<li>Signal quantification</li>\n\t<li>Protein localization</li>\n</ul>","summary":"","value":"<p>MorphoGraphX is a free Linux application for the visualization and analysis of 3D biological datasets. Developed by researchers, it is primarily used for the analysis and quantification of 3D live-imaged confocal data sets.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The main research interests adressed by MorphoGraphX are:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li>Shape extraction</li>\r\n\t<li>Growth analysis</li>\r\n\t<li>Signal quantification</li>\r\n\t<li>Protein localization</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n"}],"changed":[{"format":"Y-m-d\\TH:i:sP","value":"2020-03-03T19:54:40+00:00"}],"created":[{"format":"Y-m-d\\TH:i:sP","value":"2017-09-12T09:22:27+00:00"}],"default_langcode":[{"value":true}],"attribution_instructions":[],"comments_2023":[],"free_tagging":[],"give_feedback_on_this_soft":[{"cid":0,"comment_count":0,"last_comment_name":null,"last_comment_timestamp":1505208734,"last_comment_uid":163,"status":2}],"has_author":[{"value":"Pierre Barbier de Reuille, http://orcid.org/0000-0002-9970-765X"},{"value":"Richard S Smith, http://orcid.org/0000-0001-9220-0787"}],"has_biological_terms":[],"has_comparison":[],"has_documentation":[{"options":[],"title":"","uri":"http://www.mpipz.mpg.de/MorphoGraphX/software"}],"has_doi":[{"options":[],"title":"","uri":"http://d